xnu 0265: a ring the CP stopped consuming says so without gpudump

The wrap line was the last thing the GPU path printed before the frame path
died in ring204: 55, 57 and 44 fps, then `MESA: error: flush_submit_list:135:
submit failed: -5 (Operation not supported)` and no frame after it, with the
ring still logging. -5 is the mesa shim's default for an IOReturn it does not
know, and the only place the submission path returns one is
`mondrian_gpu_uc_submit() != 0`, whose two exits -- no room in the ring, and a
wrap whose doorbell never came back -- only printed with gpudump=1.

The no-room exit is the one worth naming on every boot: it means the CP stopped
consuming, and the numbers that say why (the write cursor, the read pointer the
poll saw, the room it computed, the sequence and how long it waited) cost one
line. Capped at eight, because a refusal repeats at the frame rate.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -4705,10 +4705,20 @@
 				break;
 			}
 			if (spent_us >= 2000000u) {
-				if (mondrian_uc_dump != 0) {
-					printf("MONDRIAN GPU: uc no room at 0x%x\n", at);
-					printf("MONDRIAN GPU: uc submit done seq %u ret %d\n",
-					    seq, -1);
+				/*
+				 * A ring the CP stopped consuming is the end of the
+				 * frame path, and until now it only said so with
+				 * gpudump=1: the client then reports "submit failed:
+				 * -5" and the reason is nowhere in the log. Print the
+				 * numbers that name it, once per occurrence, a few
+				 * times.
+				 */
+				static unsigned told;
+
+				if (told++ < 8) {
+					printf("MONDRIAN GPU: uc no room at 0x%x rptr 0x%x"
+					    " room %u seq %u after %u us\n", at, rptr, room,
+					    seq, spent_us);
 					mondrian_log_flush_now();
 				}
 				return -1;
